AmigaOS: SQLite with no fcntl() locks and Amiga path names (VOLUME:dir/file),
its temporary tables in memory, and seeks past the end of a file (which
AmigaDOS refuses on a real disk) made into reads of nothing, or into growing
the file with zeros before a write.

